Comment (collector.go:579):
Attributing CloudTrail events to load balancers via `strings.Contains(event.Raw, value)` is a loose substring match on raw JSON — short identifiers can appear inside unrelated events and mis-attribute change events to the wrong LB. Prefer matching against the structured `event.Resources` ARNs, or anchor on full ARNs only.
Replies:
reviewer conflict detected — pausing until resolved.

This conflicts with the deliberate CloudTrail attribution design: events are attached only to load balancer records and matched by load balancer ARN/resource ID or known listener ARN so listener and rule events can still be preserved without creating rule records. Restricting matching to structured `event.Resources` or full ARNs only would drop events whose relevant ELBv2 identifiers appear in CloudTrail request payloads rather than the resource list.

Please resolve the conflicting feedback and re-request review.

<!-- lisa-conflict-pending -->
Agreed — scanning the raw payload is the right call, since listener/rule events reference the LB in the request parameters rather than the structured resource list, and the identifiers being matched (full ARNs and the hashed loadBalancerID) are high-entropy enough that substring collisions are very unlikely. Withdrawing the suggestion to restrict to event.Resources. Only ask: please add a short code comment in matchEventsToLoadBalancers/eventMentions explaining why we substring-match against event.Raw, so a future reader does not "tighten" it to ARNs-only and silently drop listener/rule events.
